  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Fresh preprint and benchmark data show docking templates and confidence cutoffs now refine AlphaFold 3 and Boltz-2 antibody-complex predictions.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of AlphaFold-class predictors and curated structure-linked databases to model biomolecular interactions, with explicit evaluation of their reliability. Two items benchmark co-folding models on antibody-type complexes. PIPER rigid-body docking templates lift antibody-antigen prediction success from 56.2% to 63.4% in AlphaFold 3 and Boltz-2. A viral nanobody benchmark of Boltz-2, Chai-1 and AlphaFold3 finds AlphaFold3 leading, with ipTM and CDR3 pLDDT cutoffs helping filter predictions. CovPDB 2.0 and Propedia 26 expand curated covalent protein-ligand and protein-peptide resources, the former adding AlphaFold3 cofolding models with predicted cysteine ligandability. A host-pathogen study applies AlphaFold2/3 to 6,782 pathogen-human interactions to map molecular mimicry modes. The new element is the pairing of template augmentation and confidence-based filtering with large-scale prediction of interactions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
